        <item>
            <title>2.50.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 11:37:58 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>145</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.50.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features
- **Canopy Server**: local sessions now run in a background service on each Mac instead of inside the app window. Quitting Canopy no longer stops them, and reopening the app picks them up where they were.
- Other Macs and the iPhone can open or resume any session or folder on this Mac, not just watch sessions that are already open in a pane.
- Sessions teleported from Claude Code on the Web run in the same service.
- When Canopy updates, the service restarts onto the new build once its sessions are idle, and open panes reconnect on their own.
- Canopy now shows a banner when it lacks Full Disk Access. Without it, macOS asks for permission each time the service restarts, and sessions wait on that prompt.

### Changes
- SSH remote stays available for hosts that are not Macs (Linux, WSL, Windows).
]]></description>
